---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How the screenshots renew themselves
    accDescr: After a change of main that touches a file of .github/screenshots-paths.txt, after every release, every week and on demand, the screenshot bot looks for scripts/screenshots.sh; without it, the bot renders nothing. The script renders the pictures without secrets, and each picture whose pixels stayed the same keeps its committed file. When pixels changed and main changed none of these files while they rendered, one pull request from bot/screenshots holds the new pictures and the width and height that the pages name for them, and merges itself once every check passes; when main looks as rendered, the bot closes it. When main changed one of them meanwhile, as when the pull request before merged, or when the pull request conflicts with main later, the bot renders main anew: by itself, or started by the branch bot. So every picture shows the project as it is.

    event["`A change of main that touches<br>a file of the list, a release,<br>every week or by hand`"]
    script{"Has the repository<br>scripts/screenshots.sh?"}
    off["No script:<br>the bot renders nothing"]
    render["The script renders<br>the pictures, without secrets"]
    pixels{"Did pixels change,<br>compared with main?"}
    same["`Same pixels: the picture<br>keeps its committed file,<br>an open pull request closes`"]
    pr["`One pull request from<br>*bot/screenshots* with the<br>new sizes on the pages,<br>that merges itself`"]
    moved{"Did main change one of<br>these files while they rendered?"}
    again["`The bot renders main anew:<br>by itself, or started by<br>the branch bot after a conflict`"]
    done["Every picture shows<br>the project as it is"]

    event --> script
    script -- "no" --> off
    script -- "yes" --> render --> pixels
    pixels -- "no" --> same --> done
    pixels -- "yes" --> moved
    moved -- "no" --> pr --> done
    moved -- "yes" --> again
    pr -- "conflicts with main later" --> again
    again --> render

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class render,pr,again bot
    class off person
    class done done
